{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 264 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "1175c4b6487939c033992e27b299a883adbe1c8f1b315959d4d4f5383f9524da" :edb/db-before-t 263 :edb/db-after-t 264 :edb/tx-data [[13194139533576 50 #inst "2026-10-11T10:07:41.726Z" 13194139533576 17592186045417 true] [17592186133881 1038 #edb/ref 17592186409610 13194139533576 17592186045417 true] [17592186133898 1038 #edb/ref 17592186409609 13194139533576 17592186045417 true] [17592186134095 1068 #edb/ref 17592186130726 13194139533576 17592186045417 false] [17592186134095 1068 #edb/ref 17592186409607 13194139533576 17592186045417 true] [17592186134095 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533576 17592186045417 true] [17592186134095 1071 "Consider the vector field $F(x, y) = x\\sin yi + \\cos (xy)j$. Evaluate the scalar curl of $F$ at the point $(π, 0)$." 13194139533576 17592186045417 false] [17592186134095 1071 "Consider the vector field $F(x,y)=x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)\\,j.$ Evaluate the scalar curl of $F$ at the point $(\\pi ,0).$" 13194139533576 17592186045417 true] [17592186134095 1074 "If $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$ is a vector field on ${R}^{2}$ and the partial derivatives of the components of $F$ all exist, then the *scalar* curl of $F$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy))-\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y) \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)\\cdot y-x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y \\\\  & =-y\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)-x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the scalar curl at the point $(\\pi ,0),$ and obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})}_{(\\pi ,0)} & =-0\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi \\cdot 0)-\\pi \\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(0) \\\\  & =0-\\pi \\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533576 17592186045417 true] [17592186409590 1043 #edb/ref 17592186409611 13194139533576 17592186045417 true] [17592186409590 1043 #edb/ref 17592186409612 13194139533576 17