ef 17592186045498 13194139533576 17592186045417 true] [17592186409603 1083 #uuid "ee35c795-c099-5c49-977b-052171747158" 13194139533576 17592186045417 true] [17592186409604 1080 "-1" 13194139533576 17592186045417 true] [17592186409604 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533576 17592186045417 true] [17592186409604 1083 #uuid "f7113576-7a9c-589a-960b-40c8d014ca07" 13194139533576 17592186045417 true] [17592186409605 1080 "II and IV only" 13194139533576 17592186045417 true] [17592186409605 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533576 17592186045417 true] [17592186409605 1083 #uuid "fb3bf220-d29b-58bf-82fa-15d03e8e1406" 13194139533576 17592186045417 true] [17592186409606 1075 #edb/ref 17592186409591 13194139533576 17592186045417 true] [17592186409606 1075 #edb/ref 17592186409596 13194139533576 17592186045417 true] [17592186409606 1075 #edb/ref 17592186409598 13194139533576 17592186045417 true] [17592186409606 1075 #edb/ref 17592186409600 13194139533576 17592186045417 true] [17592186409606 1075 #edb/ref 17592186409602 13194139533576 17592186045417 true] [17592186409606 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533576 17592186045417 true] [17592186409606 1077 "selection" 13194139533576 17592186045417 true] [17592186409606 1078 #edb/ref 17592186409591 13194139533576 17592186045417 true] [17592186409606 1079 #uuid "3d405633-3d03-5b83-b9d8-c7d039eaf05b" 13194139533576 17592186045417 true] [17592186409607 1075 #edb/ref 17592186409595 13194139533576 17592186045417 true] [17592186409607 1075 #edb/ref 17592186409599 13194139533576 17592186045417 true] [17592186409607 1075 #edb/ref 17592186409601 13194139533576 17592186045417 true] [17592186409607 1075 #edb/ref 17592186409603 13194139533576 17592186045417 true] [17592186409607 1075 #edb/ref 17592186409604 13194139533576 17592186045417 true] [17592186409607 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533576 17592186045417 true] [17592186409607 1077 "selection" 13194139533576 17592186045417 true] [17592186409607 1078 #edb/ref 17592186409601 13194139533576 17592186045417 true] [17592186409607 1079 #uuid "9898eac0-330a-51e3-bb68-1c7f9a46f935" 13194139533576 17592186045417 true] [17592186409608 1075 #edb/ref 17592186409592 13194139533576 17592186045417 true] [17592186409608 1075 #edb/ref 17592186409593 13194139533576 17592186045417 true] [17592186409608 1075 #edb/ref 17592186409594 13194139533576 17592186045417 true] [17592186409608 1075 #edb/ref 17592186409597 13194139533576 17592186045417 true] [17592186409608 1075 #edb/ref 17592186409605 13194139533576 17592186045417 true] [17592186409608 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533576 17592186045417 true] [17592186409608 1077 "selection" 13194139533576 17592186045417 true] [17592186409608 1078 #edb/ref 17592186409592 13194139533576 17592186045417 true] [17592186409608 1079 #uuid "a1ff360a-7344-55e5-9541-0cbd28d2ee59" 13194139533576 17592186045417 true] [17592186409609 1068 #edb/ref 17592186409606 13194139533576 17592186045417 true] [17592186409609 1069 "q-131343" 13194139533576 17592186045417 true] [17592186409609 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533576 17592186045417 true] [17592186409609 1071 "Given that $F(x,y)=\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,i+\\frac{x}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,j,$ what is the scalar curl of $F?$" 13194139533576 17592186045417 true] [17592186409609 1072 #uuid "5a957b95-e78d-5791-8e30-44fc756d4a5e" 13194139533576 17592186045417 true] [17592186409609 1074 "If $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$ is a vector field on ${R}^{2}$ and the partial derivatives of the components of $F$ all exist, then the *scalar* curl of $F$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{x}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}})-\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}}{{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})}^{2}}-\\frac{{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}{{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2({y}^{2}-{x}^{2})}{{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533576 17592186045417 true] [17592186409610 1068 #edb/ref 17592186409608 13194139533576 17592186045417 true] [17592186409610 1069 "q-105694" 13194139533576 17592186045417 true] [17592186409610 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533576 17592186045417 true] [17592186409610 1071 "![](images/17/17637e938a25e91b9a03921dbbe0f22c8ea760f09cfed9b4a76d07bd5e3b9301.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F(x,y,z),$ shown above. Given that $F(x,y,z)$ is independent of $z,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $\\text{curl}\\,F=0$\n- $\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0$\n- $\\text{curl}\\,F$ points in the negative $z$-direction.\n- $F$ is irrotational" 13194139533576 17592186045417 true] [17592186409610 1072 #uuid "656969c6-847a-533c-a9b8-d526f82e1ab3" 13194139533576 17592186045417 true] [17592186409610 1074 "Recall that $\\text{curl}\\,F$ denotes the curl of the vector field $F.$\n\nTo understand intuitively whether a vector field has curl at a point $P$, imagine that our vector field $F$ represents the velocity field of a stream of flowing water. We place a paddlewheel at $P$ with the axis of rotation pointing in the $z$-direction, and we note whether the paddlewheel rotates or not.\n\n- If the paddlewheel is forced to rotate due to the action of the water, then the vector field has curl, i.e., $\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0.$\n\n- If the paddlewheel does not rotate due to the action of the water, then the velocity field has zero curl, i.e., $\\text{curl}\\,F=0.$\n\n![](images/f3/f385add60afac473a5734f8c1ed57c6575bada03c9c16b24fed73b200c38e2c5.png)\n\nIf $\\text{curl}\\,F=0$ everywhere in ${R}^{3}$, we say that $F$ is irrotational.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement:\n\n- Statement II is true, whereas statement I is false. If a paddlewheel were placed at any point $P$ in the manner described above, it would rotate clockwise. Therefore, $\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Using our right hand, if we wrap our fingers in the direction of rotation (clockwise), our thumb will point into the screen. Therefore, $\\text{curl}\\,F$ also points into the screen, in the direction of decreasing $z.$\n\n- Statement IV is false. Since $\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0,$ the vector field $F$ is not irrotational.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" 13194139533576 17592186045417 true] [17592186409611 1058 #edb/ref 17592186409614 13194139533576 17592186045417 true] [17592186409611 1062 #uuid "3e935ab0-b71e-5b6d-b820-ffbfd12a9752" 13194139533576 17592186045417 true] [17592186409611 1063 #edb/ref 17592186409610 13194139533576 17592186045417 true] [17592186409612 1058 #edb/ref 17592186409611 13194139533576 17592186045417 true] [17592186409612 1062 #uuid "9367b403-efcf-5ce5-86fa-9fe85e17890b" 13194139533576 17592186045417 true] [17592186409612 1063 #edb/ref 17592186241110 13194139533576 17592186045417 true] [17592186409613 1062 #uuid "94cf6f34-eb3b-582a-a36f-1fccec5bf9a0" 13194139533576 17592186045417 true] [17592186409613 1063 #edb/ref 17592186409609 13194139533576 17592186045417 true] [17592186409614 1058 #edb/ref 17592186409615 13194139533576 17592186045417 true] [17592186409614 1062 #uuid "b9f70b49-6fa6-5fee-a84d-6cdc4f073bd2" 13194139533576 17592186045417 true] [17592186409614 1063 #edb/ref 17592186134095 13194139533576 17592186045417 true] [17592186409615 1058 #edb/ref 17592186409613 13194139533576 17592186045417 true] [17592186409615 1062 #uuid "e05e6b0f-4f4c-5280-957e-b076cba38cb7" 13194139533576 17592186045417 true] [17592186409615 1063 #edb/ref 17592186262624 13194139533576 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"activity-e5b5f674-7783-5eb4-b089-af373cffcaf2" 17592186409590 "answer-0fd5ff55-9267-592c-8f53-54d27c28ddbe" 17592186409591 "answer-1524a5a3-8447-5f82-93e3-7232aaf62e6d" 17592186409592 "answer-35e57ca5-117c-5fdf-a50f-85738cb2bbce" 17592186409593 "answer-417d24bb-a5fd-5fe7-8f35-35582aaa48b4" 17592186409594 "answer-613b73ad-b4bd-580f-91d8-dabafde0761e" 17592186409595 "answer-64ee45f8-90e8-584e-9ee0-f763b1794d3a" 17592186409596 "answer-6dd98a2b-6add-530c-b212-292b094d2a67" 17592186409597 "answer-81f3041d-6679-5b2e-8990-35